// The provider CI builds for the `wasm` target with (docs/provider-targets.md).
//
// `--platform=<t>` resolves only to a target a declared provider owns, and
// the platform packages (`labelle-web`, …) are not extracted yet, so the
// Docker WASM build in ci.yml declares this package: it owns `wasm` and
// nothing else — no hooks, no commands — so the assembler still generates
// for the schema-named target exactly as before. A module plugin, because
// the assembler wires every declared package as a Zig module
// (`labelle_<name>`) and links it into the game.
.{
    .name = "wasm_fixture",
    .manifest_version = 2,
    .command_contract = ">=1.0.0 <2.0.0",
    .targets = .{"wasm"},
}
